MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 571364470}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 602e508ab3a03db42a7d1a884c3f6b31, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::CityPerson
  displayName: Dr. Hale
  nameColor: {r: 0.2, g: 0.55, b: 0.55, a: 1}
  personId: scientist_dr._hale
  firstMeeting:
  - Oh! A visitor. And those are farmer's hands, if I ever saw them. Dr. Miriam Hale, agricultural science.
  - 'Twenty years I have been trying to get a real farmer in here. I have ideas: sprinklers, gels that hold water in the soil, fertilizers that make a crop shine.'
  - Ideas cost money to test, I'm afraid. Fund the work and I will sell you whatever comes out of it at cost.
  lines:
  - Water, light, soil. Everything else is just paperwork.
  - A Platinum turnip is still a turnip. It is simply a turnip that knows its worth.
  - The river samples have been strange lately. Purple is not a colour water should be.
  - My students think food comes from a shop. Please, tell them where it comes from. Loudly.
  oneLineOnly: 0
  service: {fileID: 441307557}
  serviceLabel: Talk about research
  portraitIdle: {fileID: -1275566669, guid: f99395bd25cc9b241bb4f11919a6e6fd, type: 3}
  portraitTalk: {fileID: 1935395921, guid: f99395bd25cc9b241bb4f11919a6e6fd, type: 3}
