  groupsAtStart: 14
  linesPerPerson: {x: 1, y: 3}
  pedestrianLines:
  - Sorry, can't stop, I'm late!
  - Lovely day for it.
  - Have you tried Big Sal's hot dogs? Life-changing.
  - Is it me, or does the river smell odd lately?
  - The Sterling tower gets taller every year. Or I'm getting shorter.
  - Excuse me. Coming through.
  - You're not from the city, are you? It's the boots.
  - My cousin lives out in the suburbs. Says the bread there is amazing.
  - I work for Sterling. Everybody works for Sterling. Even the people who don't.
  - They say a scientist at the university can make it rain on one field at a time.
  - City Hall has had my form for six weeks. SIX.
  - I used to fish in that river. Nobody fishes in that river now.
  - If you see a red scooter, that's my brother. Tell him he owes me money.
  - Don't cross on Main Avenue without looking. The taxis certainly won't.
  - The treatment plant woman is the only honest person in this city. And she smells of bins.
  - Mind the litter. Or pick it up, the city pays for that now.
  - First time in the city? The museum is free on Sundays.
  - I'm not lost. I'm exploring. Slowly. In circles.
  strangerNames:
  - Passer-by
  - Commuter
  - Shopper
  - Student
  - Tourist
  - Local
